Hunspell 1.7.2 (https://github.com/hunspell/hunspell), trimmed for msga
=======================================================================

The spell checker behind msga's composer on Linux (src/spell/spell_backend_linux.cpp).
It is compiled only by the Linux branch of CMakeLists.txt, as the static library
msga_hunspell; macOS and Windows use their system spell checkers and never build it.
The dictionaries are not vendored: msga reads the ones the distribution installed
(/usr/share/hunspell, /usr/share/myspell, ...) at runtime.

License: Hunspell is tri-licensed MPL 1.1 / GPL 2.0 or later / LGPL 2.1 or later
(license.hunspell), and builds on MySpell (license.myspell). msga, GPL-3.0-or-later,
uses it under the GPL option. The copy here is a modified version: every change is
marked "msga modification" in the source and listed in msga.patch.

What is here
------------
From hunspell-1.7.2/src/hunspell only the sources the library needs:

  affentry  affixmgr  csutil  filemgr  hashmgr  hunspell  hunzip  phonet
  replist  suggestmgr                          (.cxx and .hxx of each)
  hunspell.h  hunvisapi.h  atypes.hxx  baseaffix.hxx  htypes.hxx
  langnum.hxx  w_char.hxx

Left out: the autotools files, the tools and tests, utf_info.hxx (see below) and
hunvisapi.h.in (hunvisapi.h is its output, with @HAVE_VISIBILITY@ set to 1;
HUNSPELL_STATIC, which the CMake target defines, makes the export macro empty
anyway).

What was changed (msga.patch)
-----------------------------
1. HUNSPELL_QT_UNICODE (csutil.cxx): unicodetoupper(), unicodetolower() and
   unicodeisalpha() call hunspell_qt_toupper/tolower/isalpha, which msga implements
   with QChar (spell_backend_linux.cpp), in place of the 64K-entry utf_tbl of
   utf_info.hxx: 384 KB of the binary and 2.5 MB of source, for tables Qt already
   carries. The same kind of host hook as upstream's own OPENOFFICEORG (ICU) and
   MOZILLA_CLIENT branches.
2. HUNSPELL_NO_XML (hunspell.cxx): compiles out the SPELL_XML branch of
   HunspellImpl::suggest(), the only caller of spellml(). With it the whole
   morphology/XML API (spellml, analyze, stem, generate) is unreachable, and the
   linker's section GC / LTO drops it (~90 KB).

Together with -Os and hidden visibility the library comes to about 140 KB of the
static release binary (release-linux-static.sh; stock 1.7.2 at -O2 added about
734 KB). On about 3,500 words each in en_US, ru_RU, de_DE_frami
and fa-IR (dictionary words, their case variants and generated typos) spell() and
suggest() gave byte-identical output to stock 1.7.2.

Redoing it for a new Hunspell release
-------------------------------------
  1. Unpack the release; copy the files listed above from src/hunspell/ here,
     hunvisapi.h.in as hunvisapi.h.
  2. patch -p1 < msga.patch   (run inside this directory; fix up by hand if the
     context moved: the hooks sit in the unicodeto*/unicodeisalpha functions and
     around the SPELL_XML check in HunspellImpl::suggest).
  3. Build and run tests/test_spell_check (it checks against the system en_US
     dictionary and two 8-bit test dictionaries), and compare spell/suggest
     output with a stock build on a word list if the diff touched more than the
     hooks.
  4. Regenerate msga.patch against the new stock files.
